3.1.14 Local Crisis Group
The Local Crisis Group is the body in the industrial pocket to deal with chemical
accidents and coordinate efforts in planning preparedness and mitigation of a chemical
accident;
The Local Crisis Group shall,-
1. Prepare local emergency plan for the industrial pocket;
2. Ensure dovetailing of the local emergency plan with the district off-site
emergency plan;
3. Train personnel involved in chemical accident management;
4. Educate the population likely to be affected in a chemical accident about
the remedies and existing preparedness in the area;
5. Conduct at least one full scale mock- drill of a chemical accident at a site
every six months and forward a report to the District Crisis Group;
6. Respond to all public inquiries on the subject.
